messages:
alice: Heads-up — our quickstart for the JS SDK is failing on Deno Deploy. Error: `globalThis.crypto is undefined` when calling `createClient()`

alice: We're currently importing from Skypack CDN: `import { createClient } from 'https://cdn.skypack.dev/@redwood-inference/js-sdk'` and using the default fetch flow. Works in Node, flakes in Deno/Bun.

ben: Deno and Bun have slightly different global surface. Deno expects webcrypto to be present but not always in Deploy environment. Bun has fetch but its Headers are sometimes frozen which breaks some SDK code that mutates headers.

ryan: Short fixes we used: runtime feature detection + small shims before importing SDK. Example: 
```js
if (!globalThis.crypto) {
  const mod = await import('https://deno.land/std@0.203.0/crypto/mod.ts');
  globalThis.crypto = mod.webcrypto;
}
if (!globalThis.fetch) {
  globalThis.fetch = (await import('https://esm.sh/node-fetch@3')).default;
}
```
Worked for CI and local deploys for us.

lina: For types: Deno's TypeScript environment may not include DOM libs by default. Add "lib": ["esnext","dom"] to tsconfig or in deno.json use "compilerOptions": { "lib": ["esnext", "dom"] }. Without that `CryptoKey` and `SubtleCrypto` types are missing.

ben: We should consider publishing a `deno/` entrypoint bundle that only relies on Web APIs (no Node builtins) and a small README listing required globals. That avoids CDN import quirks and makes onboarding smoother.

edge-bot: note: intermittent test failures in Bun CI for `auth retry` suite. Looks like timing of 429 backoffs differs on Bun's networking layer. Filing flaky ticket.

ryan: In the SDK, small defensive changes help: don't mutate incoming Headers, wrap retry timeouts with configurable backoff, and detect frozen headers via `Object.isFrozen(headers)` before attempting mutations. Also expose a `platform` option so callers can opt into runtime-specific tweaks: `createClient({ platform: 'deno' })`.

alice: I'll prototype a `deno` bundle and a short snippet in our quickstart showing the shims. If we add a published `dist/deno/index.mjs` we can reference it in import_map and avoid CDN transformation issues.

lina: Also add example `globals.d.ts` to the bundle so users get types without editing tsconfig: 
```ts
declare global {
  var crypto: Crypto;
  var fetch: typeof globalThis.fetch;
}
export {};
```

ben: Sounds good. Filing a short RFC for `deno` entry and runtime tests for Bun/Deno. I'll link the flaky CI job in the RFC. :+1:

alice: thanks all, will drop a minimal repro if the deno bundle doesn't resolve it.
